        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Routes normal NL requests through classification and Insight bossExtract requests through query spoofing.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Check Object Determination"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "linear_1004_scope_classifier",
            "false": "linear_1801_prepare_journal_query_spoof_state"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_CONDITION_CHECK_OBJECT_DETERMINATION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "linear_1804_determine_journal_data_retrieval_type",
          "id": "linear_1401_check_immediate_execution",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "linear_1401_check_object_determination_condition",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.performObjectDetermination === true}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Classifies the request scope and journal inquiry type.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Classify Request Scope"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1006_if_out_of_scope"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_SCOPE_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "linear_1004_scope_classifier",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776123913355_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict request classifier for a Journals Inquiry Assistant.\n\nClassify the current user request using USER_INPUT and CHAT_HISTORY.\nReturn exactly one minified JSON object and nothing else.\n\nPurpose:\n\t1. Decide whether the request is IN_SCOPE or OUT_OF_SCOPE.\n\t2. If IN_SCOPE, decide whether it is a SUMMARY request or DETAIL request.\n\t3. Provide a concise justification.\n\nIN_SCOPE means journal inquiry and journal data retrieval only, including:\n\t- journal summaries, totals, counts, activity, net activity, grouped output, and breakdowns\n\t- journal details, journal headers, journal lines, full journal entries, and journal action-log inquiry\n\t- journal source, journal category, batch, journal name, period, ledger, accounting date, status, approval status, and COA-segment journal inquiry\n\t- follow-up questions that clearly continue a prior in-scope journal inquiry\n\t- pure sort/order-by follow-ups that clearly continue a prior in-scope journal inquiry\n\t- balance-to-journal follow-ups that ask for journals, journal details, journal lines, journal entries, journal source/category contribution, or transactions contributing to a prior balance\n\nOUT_OF_SCOPE includes:\n\t- Non-journal questions:\n\t\t- Requests that are not asking for journal inquiry or journal data retrieval.\n\t\t- This includes pure balance inquiries that do not ask for journal contribution or journal retrieval, subledger/payables/receivables-only requests, help/how-to questions, definitions, configuration, setup, schedules, process topics\n\t\t- Operational tasks such as posting, approving, reversing, creating, updating, deleting, or submitting journals.\n\t- Multiple financial objects:\n\t\t- The financial object categories are Balance, Journal, and Subledger.\n\t\t- If the current USER_INPUT requests more than one category, classify it as `OUT_OF_SCOPE`.\n\t\t- Identify only the objects explicitly requested. Do not infer reports, breakdowns, fields, filters, dimensions, optional steps, or other objects.\n\t\t- Count a financial object only when the USER asks for records or measures from that object as a distinct part of the current request. A term used only as a journal source, import origin, filter, property, or prior context does not add another financial object.\n\t\t- Examples: \"journals imported from subledgers\" is Journal only; \"Payables transactions and their General Ledger journals\" is Subledger and Journal; \"journals where all lines are balanced\" is Journal only.\n\t\t- Preserve the order or dependency stated by the USER.\n\t\t- For multiple financial objects, set `justification` to one plain-text guidance message with no newline characters:\n\t\t\t- Two objects: `This request combines a <first object> inquiry and a <second object> inquiry. As a follow-up, ask for <first object> first, then ask for <second object> as a separate follow-up.`\n\t\t\t- Three objects: `This request combines balance, journal, and subledger inquiries. As a follow-up, ask for each inquiry separately in the order stated.`\n\t\t- Use the USER's object wording when clear, such as \"balance\", \"contributing journals\", or \"Payables transactions\". Otherwise, use object name.\n\t\t- Include a concise split path derived from the USER request when it is clear. Do not invent unsupported filters, fields, or follow-up details.\n\t- Trend or explanatory analysis:\n\t\t- Classify as `OUT_OF_SCOPE` only when the USER asks for causes, drivers, explanations, predictions, recommendations, or open-ended trend or pattern interpretation across journal data.\n\t\t- Multiple periods, a date range, grouping by period, a direct comparison, or a deterministic derived condition do not by themselves make a request trend analysis.\n\t\t- Keep concrete journal retrieval requests `IN_SCOPE` when they contain percentages, averages, rankings, duplicate checks, record-count conditions, no-activity conditions, consecutive-period conditions, set differences, or similar defined predicates; do not treat them as trend analysis.\n\t\t- Keep subjective, risk, anomaly, or undefined journal-retrieval wording `IN_SCOPE` when the USER asks to show, find, list, or check journals, postings, or journal activity. Examples include abnormal, unusual, suspicious, irregular, unexpected, or odd. Do not classify these as trend or explanatory analysis unless the USER explicitly asks for a narrative explanation, cause, driver, prediction, or recommendation.\n\t\t- For `OUT_OF_SCOPE`, set `justification` to: `This request asks for trend or explanatory analysis across journal data. Ask for the underlying journal data first, then review the returned results separately.`\n\nClassification rules:\n\t- Apply OUT_OF_SCOPE rules before IN_SCOPE request-type rules.\n\t- Apply the Multiple Financial Objects rule to the current USER_INPUT before any follow-up exception.\n\t- The balance-to-journal exception applies only when the current USER_INPUT asks for journals alone and CHAT_HISTORY contains the prior balance request or result.\n\t- Do not classify a journal-only follow-up as multiple-object merely because CHAT_HISTORY contains a balance.\n\t- A current request that asks for both a balance and contributing journals is OUT_OF_SCOPE. A current journal-only request that follows a prior balance result may be IN_SCOPE.\n\t- If USER_INPUT matches an OUT_OF_SCOPE rule, return OUT_OF_SCOPE even if it contains journal words such as journal, journal activity, journal source, journal lines, or journal entries.\n\t- Treat inquiry/retrieval requests as IN_SCOPE even when phrased as show, list, get, inspect, find, display, summarize, total, count, or break down and do not match an OUT_OF_SCOPE rule.\n\t- Treat journal operational action requests as OUT_OF_SCOPE even if they mention journals.\n\t- For journal operational actions such as posting, approval, reversal, create, update, submit, or delete, set justification exactly to \"unsupported journal action\".\n\t- Treat action-log, workflow history, audit, lifecycle, who performed an action, or when an action happened as IN_SCOPE DETAIL.\n\t- Treat pure balance questions as OUT_OF_SCOPE, but treat balance-to-journal contribution follow-ups as IN_SCOPE.\n\t- Do not classify a follow-up as multiple-financial-object solely because prior CHAT_HISTORY contains a different financial object.\n\t- If USER_INPUT is underspecified but clearly continues a prior in-scope journal inquiry, use CHAT_HISTORY only to classify the continuation.\n\t- Treat pure sort/order-by follow-ups as IN_SCOPE when CHAT_HISTORY shows a prior in-scope journal inquiry. Preserve the prior journal request type when it is clear from CHAT_HISTORY.\n\t- If the USER asks for journal records or journal activity with a subjective condition, classify it as `IN_SCOPE`; the subjective condition should be clarified later by NER.\n\t- If uncertain, prefer OUT_OF_SCOPE.\n\nRequest type rules for IN_SCOPE:\n\t- Determine SUMMARY or DETAIL from the requested result shape, not merely from words used inside a filter or derived condition.\n\t- SUMMARY when the resolved request asks for aggregation, summary, aggregate, total, sum, count, average, journal activity, net activity, top/highest contributing journal sources, top journal source, grouped output, split, breakdown, or \"by <dimension>\" output.\n\t- Activity and aggregation precedence: when the resolved request contains activity, journal activity, net activity, summary, breakdown, aggregate, total, sum, count, top/highest contributing journal sources, top journal source, grouping, split, or \"by <dimension>\" intent, classify as SUMMARY even when phrased with show, list, get, inspect, find, or display.\n\t- Do not let filters such as posting status, approval status, journal source, legal entity, period, date range, currency, account, COA segment, or other filter values turn an activity/aggregation request into DETAIL.\n\t- Only override an activity/aggregation SUMMARY to DETAIL when USER_INPUT explicitly asks for journal lines, journal entries, journal headers, journal details, full journal entry, action logs, or other detail or record-level rows.\n\t- SUMMARY for balance-to-journal follow-ups only when USER_INPUT explicitly asks for summary, total, aggregate, breakdown, grouping, journal source/category contribution, or net activity.\n\t- DETAIL for list/show/get/inspect journals, journal headers, journal details, journal lines, journal entries, full journal entry, action logs, or any record-level journal inquiry, except when the activity and aggregation precedence rule applies.\n\t- DETAIL for balance-to-journal follow-ups asking for journals, lines, journal details, journal entries, or transactions contributing to a balance unless the current user explicitly asks for summary/grouping/breakdown/net activity.\n\t- For pure sort/order-by follow-ups, classify as SUMMARY when the prior journal inquiry in CHAT_HISTORY was summary, total, count, activity, grouped output, split, or breakdown; classify as DETAIL when the prior journal inquiry was record-level journals, details, lines, headers, entries, or action logs.\n\t- If in scope and not clearly SUMMARY, classify as DETAIL.\n\nOutput schema:\n\t- OUT_OF_SCOPE: {\"scope\":\"OUT_OF_SCOPE\",\"justification\":\"<concise justification>\"}\n\t- IN_SCOPE: {\"scope\":\"IN_SCOPE\",\"request_type\":\"SUMMARY\"|\"DETAIL\",\"justification\":\"<concise justification>\"}\n\nHard rules:\n\t- Output exactly one JSON object\n\t- No markdown\n\t- No explanation\n\t- No extra keys\n\t- No trailing text\n\t- No nulls\n\nCHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.chatHistory}}\n\nUSER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.userInput}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"oneOf\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"scope\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"request_type\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"SUMMARY\",\n            \"DETAIL\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"justification\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"scope\",\n        \"justification\"\n      ],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"scope\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"IN_SCOPE\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"request_type\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"SUMMARY\",\n            \"DETAIL\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"justification\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"scope\",\n        \"request_type\",\n        \"justification\"\n      ],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Builds normal query state from Insights bossExtract so data retrieval can use the journal execution path.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Prepare Reused Query State",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const isObject = (value) => value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\nconst asArray = (value) => (Array.isArray(value) ? value : []);\n\nconst firstObjectValue = (value) => {\n  let result = new Object();\n\n  if (isObject(value)) {\n    const firstKey = Object.keys(value)[0];\n    result = firstKey && isObject(value[firstKey]) ? value[firstKey] : value;\n  }\n\n  return result;\n};\n\nconst normalizeQueries = (value) => {\n  let normalizedQueries = [];\n\n  if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    normalizedQueries = value;\n  } else if (isObject(value)) {\n    normalizedQueries = [value];\n  }\n\n  return normalizedQueries;\n};\n\nconst allowedAv = \"ora_erp_core_accountedTransactions_runtime_x__JournalSummary\";\nconst allowedAvModule = \"oraErpCoreAccountedTransactionsRuntime\";\nconst allowedBvModule = \"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\";\nconst allowedBvs = {\n  generalLedgerJournalDetail: \"JournalLine\",\n  journalActionLogDetails: \"JournalActionLog\",\n  journalHeaderDetail: \"JournalHeader\"\n};\n\nconst getBusinessViewDescriptor = (query) => {\n  let descriptor = new Object();\n\n  if (isObject(query?.target)) {\n    descriptor = query.target;\n  } else if (isObject(query?.viewQueries)) {\n    descriptor = Object.values(query.viewQueries).find((viewQuery) => {\n      if (!isObject(viewQuery)) {\n        return false;\n      }\n\n      const businessView = viewQuery.businessView ?? viewQuery.view;\n      return viewQuery.module === allowedBvModule && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(allowedBvs, businessView);\n    }) ?? new Object();\n  }\n\n  return descriptor;\n};\n\nconst normalizeMetadata = (metadata) => (isObject(metadata) ? metadata : new Object());\n\nconst hasCoaSegments = (metadata) => {\n  const segments = normalizeMetadata(metadata).chartOfAccounts?.segments;\n  return isObject(segments) && Object.keys(segments).length > 0;\n};\n\nconst mergeMetadataWithAvExtractFallback = (baseMetadata, fallbackMetadata) => {\n  const base = normalizeMetadata(baseMetadata);\n  const fallback = normalizeMetadata(fallbackMetadata);\n\n  if (hasCoaSegments(base) || !hasCoaSegments(fallback)) {\n    return base;\n  }\n\n  return {\n    ...fallback,\n    ...base,\n    chartOfAccounts: {\n      ...normalizeMetadata(fallback.chartOfAccounts),\n      ...normalizeMetadata(base.chartOfAccounts),\n      segments: fallback.chartOfAccounts.segments\n    }\n  };\n};\n\nconst getAvExtractMetadataCandidates = (parsedInput, additionalContext) => {\n  const inputState = normalizeMetadata(parsedInput.inputState);\n  const privateState = normalizeMetadata(inputState.private);\n  const legacyDomainSlice = normalizeMetadata(inputState.domainSlice);\n  const domains = normalizeMetadata(inputState.domains);\n  const candidates = [\n    additionalContext?.avExtractResult?.metadata,\n    additionalContext?.dataResponse?.avExtractResult?.metadata,\n    parsedInput.dataResponse?.avExtractResult?.metadata,\n    privateState.lastUsedData?.dataResponse?.avExtractResult?.metadata,\n    legacyDomainSlice.lastUsedData?.dataOutput?.data?.avExtractResult?.metadata,\n    legacyDomainSlice.lastUsedData?.dataResponse?.avExtractResult?.metadata\n  ];\n\n  for (const domainName of Object.keys(domains)) {\n    candidates.push(domains[domainName]?.lastUsedData?.dataResponse?.avExtractResult?.metadata);\n  }\n\n  return candidates;\n};\n\nconst resolveMetadata = (baseMetadata, parsedInput, additionalContext) => {\n  let resolvedMetadata = normalizeMetadata(baseMetadata);\n\n  for (const candidate of getAvExtractMetadataCandidates(parsedInput, additionalContext)) {\n    resolvedMetadata = mergeMetadataWithAvExtractFallback(resolvedMetadata, candidate);\n    if (hasCoaSegments(resolvedMetadata)) {\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return resolvedMetadata;\n};\n\nconst parsedInput = $context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT?.$output?.result ?? new Object();\nconst additionalContext = parsedInput.additionalContext ?? $context.$triggers.REST.$input.additionalContext;\nconst bossExtract = additionalContext.bossExtract;\nconst queries = normalizeQueries(bossExtract.queries);\nconst firstQuery = queries[0] ?? new Object();\nconst contextQuery = additionalContext.queries?.[0]?.query ?? new Object();\nconst userQuestion = String(parsedInput.userInput || $context.$system.$inputMessage || bossExtract.question || \"\");\nconst queryTitle = String(userQuestion || bossExtract.question || \"Journal insight\").slice(0, 100);\nconst analyticViewDescriptor = firstObjectValue(firstQuery?.analyticViews);\nconst businessViewDescriptor = getBusinessViewDescriptor(firstQuery);\nconst isAv =\n  additionalContext.queryType === \"avExtract\" ||\n  additionalContext.queryType === \"avWorkflow\" ||\n  (additionalContext.queryType !== \"bvExtract\" && Boolean(analyticViewDescriptor.name));\nconst errors = [];\nlet queryPayload = new Object();\nlet analyticViewNameUsed = \"\";\nlet businessViewNameUsed = \"\";\n\nif (isAv) {\n  const moduleName = analyticViewDescriptor.module;\n  const analyticView = analyticViewDescriptor.name;\n\n  if (!analyticView) {\n    errors.push(\"additionalContext.bossExtract.queries.analyticViews must include a journal summary analytic view object.\");\n  }\n  if (!moduleName) {\n    errors.push(\"additionalContext.bossExtract.queries.analyticViews must include module.\");\n  }\n  if (moduleName && moduleName !== allowedAvModule) {\n    errors.push(\"Insight analytic view module must be oraErpCoreAccountedTransactionsRuntime.\");\n  }\n  if (analyticView && analyticView !== allowedAv) {\n    errors.push(\"Insight analytic view must be the journal summary analytic view.\");\n  }\n\n  analyticViewNameUsed = allowedAv;\n  const query = new Object();\n  const filter = contextQuery.filter ?? analyticViewDescriptor.filter ?? firstQuery.filter ?? \"\";\n  if (typeof filter === \"string\" && filter.trim() !== \"\") {\n    query.filter = filter;\n  }\n\n  const queryEntry = {\n    analyticView: allowedAv,\n    module: allowedAvModule,\n    ledgerContext: additionalContext?.ledgerContext,\n    query,\n    time_period: asArray(contextQuery.time_period)\n  };\n  if (additionalContext.ledgerCategory !== undefined && additionalContext.ledgerCategory !== null && additionalContext.ledgerCategory !== \"\") {\n    queryEntry.ledgerCategory = additionalContext.ledgerCategory;\n  }\n\n  queryPayload = {\n    targetObject: \"journals_av\",\n    userQuestion,\n    directLLM: false,\n    chartOfAccountsId: String(additionalContext.chartOfAccountsId ?? \"\"),\n    queries: [queryEntry],\n    additionalInfo: {\n      processExecutionId: String(additionalContext.processExecutionId ?? \"\")\n    }\n  };\n} else {\n  const moduleName = businessViewDescriptor.module;\n  const businessObject = businessViewDescriptor.businessObject;\n  const businessView = businessViewDescriptor.businessView ?? businessViewDescriptor.view;\n\n  if (!businessView) {\n    errors.push(\"additionalContext.bossExtract.queries.viewQueries must include a supported journal business view object.\");\n  }\n  if (!moduleName) {\n    errors.push(\"Insight business view query must include module.\");\n  }\n  if (!businessObject) {\n    errors.push(\"Insight business view query must include businessObject.\");\n  }\n  if (moduleName && moduleName !== allowedBvModule) {\n    errors.push(\"Insight business view module must be oraErpCoreAccountingEntries.\");\n  }\n  if (businessView && !Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(allowedBvs, businessView)) {\n    errors.push(\"Insight business view must be a supported journal detail view.\");\n  }\n  if (businessView && allowedBvs[businessView] && businessObject && allowedBvs[businessView] !== businessObject) {\n    errors.push(\"Insight business object does not match the journal detail view.\");\n  }\n\n  businessViewNameUsed = businessView || \"\";\n  queryPayload = {\n    targetObject: \"journals_bv\",\n    queryTitle,\n    userQuestion,\n    directLLM: false,\n    taskType: \"NL2BQL-GENERIC\",\n    includeHeaderOnly: \"\",\n    chartOfAccountsId: additionalContext.chartOfAccountsId ?? 0,\n    templateId: additionalContext.templateId ?? \"\",\n    queries: [\n      {\n        businessView,\n        businessObject,\n        module: moduleName,\n        ledgerContext: additionalContext?.ledgerContext,\n        query: {\n          filter: contextQuery.filter ?? firstQuery?.query?.collection?.filter ?? \"\"\n        },\n        ledgerCategory: additionalContext.ledgerCategory ?? \"\",\n        time_period: asArray(contextQuery.time_period),\n        currency: Array.isArray(contextQuery.currency) ? contextQuery.currency[0] ?? \"\" : typeof contextQuery.currency === \"string\" ? contextQuery.currency : \"\"\n      }\n    ],\n    dataGrain: \"\",\n    additionalInfo: {\n      processExecutionId: additionalContext.processExecutionId ?? \"\"\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nif (!isAv && additionalContext.templateDetails !== undefined && additionalContext.templateDetails !== null && additionalContext.templateDetails !== \"\") {\n  queryPayload.templateDetails = additionalContext.templateDetails;\n}\nif (!isAv && additionalContext.allPlaceholdersSelected !== undefined && additionalContext.allPlaceholdersSelected !== null && additionalContext.allPlaceholdersSelected !== \"\") {\n  queryPayload.allPlaceholdersSelected = additionalContext.allPlaceholdersSelected;\n}\n\nconst queryResponse = {\n  timeStamp: bossExtract?.timeStamp ?? bossExtract?.timestamp ?? new Date().toISOString(),\n  question: bossExtract?.question ?? userQuestion,\n  intentRecognition: bossExtract?.intentRecognition ?? true,\n  metadata: resolveMetadata(bossExtract?.metadata ?? additionalContext.metadata, parsedInput, additionalContext),\n  queries\n};\n\nconst returnObj = {\n  valid: errors.length === 0,\n  errors,\n  queryPayload,\n  queryResponse,\n  queryTitle,\n  analyticViewNameUsed,\n  businessViewNameUsed,\n  coaBreakdown: []\n};\n\nreturn returnObj;"
          },
