          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1017_determine_coa_breakdown_needed"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_CODE_SELECT_SUMMARY_VIEW",
          "id": "linear_1014_select_analytic_view",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Builds the detail userQuestion/queryTitle and determines all-journal-lines intent in one LLM call.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Analyze Detail and Lines Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1203_determine_journal_detail_scope_change"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYZE_DETAIL_AND_LINES_INTENT",
          "id": "linear_1201_rephrase_journal_detail_question",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "linear_1201_rephrase_journal_detail_question_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Role & objective\nYou are a strict detail-question and all-lines-intent analyzer for a Journals Inquiry Assistant.\nReturn exactly one minified JSON object and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs:\nCHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.chatHistory}}\n\nUSER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.userInput}}\n\nTURN_CONTEXT:\n{\n  ledgerContext: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.ledgerContext}},\n  selectedHierarchies: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.selectedHierarchies}},\n  scopeChange: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.scopeChange}}\n}\n\nACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  analyticViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed}},\n  businessViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}},\n  queryResponse: {{$context.$variables.queryResponse}},\n  dataResponse: {{$context.$variables.dataResponse}},\n  coaBreakdown: {{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}}\n}\n\n## Core behavior:\n- Rephrase, do not interpret.\n- Frame one meaningful, complete journal question based on the current USER intent, preserving the current USER entities, filters, conditions, and intent as-is. For short follow-ups, preserve the meaning but do not preserve fragment wording.\n- Add only missing context from prior USER inputs when still applicable and not replaced, contradicted, or made irrelevant by the current USER input.\n- Do not paraphrase, normalize, infer, map, summarize, group, resolve, or transform USER terms.\n- Do not include technical/context JSON.\n\n## First question behavior:\n- If this is the first USER question in the conversation, return the USER_INPUT as-is as the final question, except replace double quotes with single quotes.\n- Do not add context from prior messages, TURN_CONTEXT, ACTIVE_STATE, assistant messages, tool outputs, or result data for the first question.\n\n## Source of truth:\n- Use ONLY values explicitly mentioned in current or prior USER inputs, except journalName or batchName values from ACTIVE_STATE when resolving explicit references to prior journal or batch results under the Carry-forward rules.\n- TURN_CONTEXT and ACTIVE_STATE may be used only to detect flow state when needed; they must not be used as sources for filters, values, rows, currencies, ledgers, periods, amounts, identifiers, or wording in the final question, except to resolve explicit references to prior journal or batch results under the Carry-forward rules.\n- DO NOT pick values from AI-generated titles, headlines, displayed rows, result rows, row headers, child/detail rows, parent rows, intent-confirmation blocks, tool outputs, currentLevelAvData, childLevelAvData, measure result values, prior returned table cells, or assistant text, except to resolve the referenced journal or batch identifier(s) under the Carry-forward rules.\n- Current USER input has highest precedence for fields/entities/anchors it mentions. Add new current fields, replace prior values only for the same field, and keep unrelated prior USER-mentioned filters unless the current USER explicitly removes or changes them.\n- The latest USER-mentioned value for the same field/entity replaces earlier values unless the user asks to include multiple values.\n- Never invent missing filters, anchors, dates, ledgers, currencies, statuses, COA values, or identifiers.\n\n## Carry-forward rules:\n- For follow-ups, carry forward only applicable scope anchors explicitly mentioned in prior USER inputs when the current USER input is silent about that same field/anchor. A current USER value for one field/anchor replaces only that same field/anchor and does not remove unrelated prior USER-mentioned filters.\n- Scope anchors include but not limited to: accounting period/date/date ranges, ledger, journal/approval status, source, category, legal entity, currency if user-mentioned, COA filters, journal/batch identifiers, amount filters, breakdown dimensions, and explicit sort/order-by fields and order.\n- Carry forward the prior USER-mentioned base journal intent when needed, such as journal activity, summary, journals, details, lines, or entries.\n- If the current USER input corrects prior USER wording, such as \"I meant X not Y\", reframe the still-applicable prior USER question with the correction applied and do not include the correction phrase itself in the final question.\n- When rephrasing a follow-up, replace indirect references such as \"above journal\", \"this journal\", \"that journal\", or \"selected journal\" with only the applicable journalName or batchName from ACTIVE_STATE. Do not keep both the indirect reference and the resolved value.\n- Use ACTIVE_STATE only to resolve distinct journalName or batchName values. Do not copy ledger, period, dates, COA values, account combinations, source, category, currency, status, amounts, users, action codes, totals, or any other result-row values.\n- If the USER explicitly asks for batch or journal batch, resolve the reference in the rephrased question as journal batch '<batchName>' using distinct batchName values from ACTIVE_STATE. Never use journalName as a batch value.\n- If the USER asks for action, workflow, audit, approval, approver, created by, posted by, submitted by, action history, action log, or actor/user information, resolve any indirect journal reference in the rephrased question as journal batch '<batchName>' using distinct batchName values from ACTIVE_STATE when available. This takes precedence over prior USER-mentioned journal identifiers. If no batchName is available, use the safest prior USER-mentioned identifier exactly as stated.\n- For other indirect journal references, resolve the reference as journal '<journalName>' using distinct journalName values from ACTIVE_STATE.\n- Preserve existing journal-attribute filters and breakdowns unless the current USER replaces, removes, contradicts, or changes them.\n- Preserve explicit user-mentioned sort/order-by fields and order unless the current USER replaces, removes, contradicts, or changes them. Do not add implicit sort wording for breakdown requests.\n- If the current USER input adds values using wording such as also/include/both, accumulate those values.\n- If values conflict, use the current USER input value.\n- Ledger and accounting period/date filters must be carried forward only when explicitly mentioned in prior USER inputs and the current USER input is silent about them, unless the current USER explicitly changes or drops them.\n- Do not carry forward ledger or accounting period/date values merely because they appear in TURN_CONTEXT, ACTIVE_STATE, assistant text, tool output, or result data.\n\n## Rephrasing guardrails:\nWhen framing or rephrasing the current user question:\n\nDO NOT:\n- Add clarifications, explanations, parenthetical expansions, synonyms, semantic equivalents, qualifiers, business terms, or inferred filters.\n- Generalize or specialize any term.\n- Convert detail/list requests into summary/aggregate/breakdown requests, or summary/aggregate/breakdown requests into detail/list requests unless the user explicitly asks for it.\n- Convert a currency descriptor into a currency breakdown unless the user explicitly asks to break down, group, summarize, or show by currency.\n- Derive or carry forward filters from prior headlines, displayed table rows, row headers, child/detail rows, parent rows, tool result rows, `childLevelAvData`, `currentLevelAvData`, or measure result values.\n- Alter, split, tokenize, or reinterpret text enclosed in single ('...') or double (\"...\") quotes (treat the full quoted string as an atomic identifier and preserve it exactly in the rephrased question, except that double quote characters must be replaced with single quote characters in the final output).\n- Leave out user-specified values, including COA segment values, batch names, journal names, transaction numbers, journal source, journal category, account combinations, currency terms, or line descriptions, unless explicitly requested to be dropped.\n- Drop or replace existing journal-attribute breakdown/grouping dimensions unless the user explicitly says to replace/remove them.\n- Rewrite, normalize, or substitute status/control phrases. Preserve these phrases EXACTLY as stated in the user input or valid carried context, such as \"without approvals\", \"not approved\", \"unapproved\", \"not posted\", \"pending\", \"posted\", etc.\n- Add posting status unless it was explicitly mentioned in current or still-applicable prior USER input, except when the balance-to-journal follow-up rule explicitly allows adding \"posted journals\" or \"posted journal lines\".\n- Append filters or statuses as detached trailing fragments. The final output must be one natural, grammatically complete question.\n- Include entered currency, ledger currency, currency code, currency symbols, or any currency-related wording while rephrasing UNLESS that exact currency wording was explicitly mentioned in the current or prior USER input. Do not infer it from balance responses, intent-confirmation text, tool filters, result rows, monetary templates, ledger currency, or examples.\n- Carry forward terms like aggregate/summary/total from prior user inputs unless explicitly mentioned by the user in the current input or required by an active prior USER-requested breakdown/summary context.\n- Carry forward prior COA segment filters, account combination filters, or COA segment breakdowns for journal details/lines/entries for a specific journal/batch unless the current user explicitly repeats them.\n\nONLY:\n- Fix only minimal grammar or word-order issues required to make the final output a valid question, without changing USER wording, business terms, filters, values, conditions, or intent.\n- Carry forward filters, entities, conditions, and breakdowns exactly as stated, subject to these guardrails.\n- Apply entity replacement across USER messages first: the most recent USER-mentioned value for the same field/entity replaces any earlier value unless the user explicitly asks to include multiple values.\n- Preserve quoted text as one atomic identifier, except that double quote characters must be replaced with single quote characters in the final output.\n- ALWAYS replace any double quotes (\"..\") in the final userQuestion with single quotes ('..') and NEVER introduce double quotes in the final userQuestion.\n\n## Calendar and date handling:\n- Preserve temporal expressions exactly as stated.\n- Do not resolve relative dates or periods into absolute dates, calendar ranges, accounting periods, or labels.\n- Do not convert fiscal-period-shaped values such as Feb-26, Mar-26, or May-26 into calendar dates or date ranges during rephrasing.\n- If the USER names a date field, preserve that date-field wording.\n- If the current USER input is silent about period/date range or ledger, carry forward prior applicable USER-mentioned period/date range or ledger.\n- Do not default period/date range from current date, system date, context JSON, or tool output.\n\n## Journal/batch-specific detail exception\n- Before general carry-forward, if the current USER asks for journal details/lines/entries for one or more specific journals, batches, or referenced prior journals/batches:\n\t- Rephrase using the journal/batch identifier from the current USER input as the primary filter, preserving the identifier exactly.\n\t- Preserve prior USER-mentioned period/date range and ledger when the current USER is silent.\n\t- Drop prior USER-mentioned COA segment filters, COA value filters such as account, company, cost center, account-combination filters, and COA breakdowns unless the current USER repeats those same COA filters in the current message.\n\t- Preserve identifier type exactly when the USER states one. If the USER does not specify journal, header, batch, or journal batch, do not introduce a new identifier type.\n\t- Do not derive or carry forward COA filters from assistant headlines, displayed table rows, row headers, prior journal rows, balance result rows, parent rows, child rows, `currentLevelAvData`, `childLevelAvData`, tool result rows, or measure result values.\n\t- Example:\n\t\t- Prior USER: `show balance for 11010 account in Mar-26 period`\n\t\t- Prior USER: `Export to Excel`\n\t\t- Current USER: `Show journal details for journal batch '3899-FR_Manual_ FR Manual Source A 44309 N'`\n\t\t- Correct rephrased question: `Show journal details for journal batch '3899-FR_Manual_ FR Manual Source A 44309 N' in Mar-26`\n\t\t- Incorrect rephrased question: `Show journal details for journal batch '3899-FR_Manual_ FR Manual Source A 44309 N'`\n\t\t- Incorrect rephrased question: `Show journal details for journal batch '3899-FR_Manual_ FR Manual Source A 44309 N' in Apr-26`\n\n## Balance-to-journal follow-up rules:\n- Apply this section only when the current request is a balance-to-journal follow-up and a prior successful balance response exists in chat history.\n- A prior successful balance response may be used only to detect that the current request is a balance-to-journal follow-up. It must not be used as a source for filters, values, rows, currencies, ledgers, periods, amounts, or identifiers.\n- Remove any numeric comparison, threshold, or range conditions on balance/amount measures that originated in prior turns unless the current USER input specifies a new journal amount condition.\n- Remove inherited amount expressions using comparators such as greater than, more than, over, at least, less than, under, at most, between, equals, not equals, and operators like >, <, >=, <=, =, !=.\n- Remove inherited amount expressions with currency symbols/codes before or after the number, optional spaces, and number formatting such as commas, periods, or thin spaces. Examples: greater than 5000, lesser than 3,000 USD, > $3,000, between EUR 2,000 and 5,000, at most GBP 4,500.50.\n- If the current USER specifies a new journal amount condition, KEEP it.\n- For balance-to-journal follow-ups, carry forward prior USER-mentioned non-amount balance scope filters, including account/COA, company, period/date, ledger, legal entity, and currency wording when explicitly user-mentioned, unless the current USER replaces that same field. Do not carry forward amount filters unless the current USER specifies a new journal amount condition.\n- Carry forward currency wording only when explicitly mentioned in a USER input.\n- Do not reinterpret balance amount conditions as journal amount conditions.\n- Do not carry currency from balance context unless currency was explicitly mentioned in current or prior USER inputs/messages.\n- Do not use balance result rows, headlines, tool outputs, intent-confirmation text, context JSON, or measure values as journal filters.\n- The rephrased question must preserve the user’s current input and intent, plus only valid carried-forward context.\n\n## Journal status for balance-to-journal follow-ups ONLY\n- Apply this section ONLY when the current input is a journal-related follow-up from a prior successful BALANCE response.\n- Do NOT apply this section when the prior successful response was already journal-related, including journal amounts, activity, net activity, summaries, batches, lines, details, or entries.\n- Status handling:\n\t- Every valid balance-to-journal follow-up must include a posting status.\n\t- If the current USER input mentions a posting status, preserve it exactly.\n\t- Otherwise, add the default status \"posted\".\n- Object handling for valid balance-to-journal follow-ups:\n\t- Preserve the journal object requested by the current USER input.\n\t- For example:\n\t\t- If the USER asks for Journal Batches, use \"posted Journal Batches\".\n\t\t- If the USER asks for Journals or contributing journals, use \"posted journals\".\n\t\t- If the USER asks for Journal Lines, Journal Details, Journal Entries, line details, or line descriptions, use \"posted journal lines\".\n\t\t- If the USER does not specify a journal object and asks usage/detail questions such as \"where was this used\", \"show usage\", \"show details\", or \"show/list contributing details\" and if the current or prior user question has COA or line level intent then also use \"posted journal lines\".\n- Hard boundary:\n\t- Never infer or add \"posted\" outside valid balance-to-journal follow-ups.\n\t- Never replace, normalize, or override a USER-mentioned posting status.\n\t- Never use assistant messages, result rows, table headers, tool outputs, ACTIVE_STATE, or TURN_CONTEXT as a source for posting status.\n\t\n## All-lines intent rules:\n- Set allJournalLinesIntent to allJournalLines only when the current user input to display/view full/all journal lines, journal details, journal entries, full journal entry, full journal details, all journal lines, full journal lines, or line-level data for a specific journal/batch or set of journals/batches.\n- This applies even when the user says journal details rather than all journal lines, if a specific journal or batch identifier is present.\n- Do not set allJournalLinesIntent to allJournalLines when the current USER input asks for action, workflow, audit, or actor information rather than journal line/detail content.\n- Do not set allJournalLinesIntent for generic balance-to-journal follow-ups without a specific journal/batch identifier.\n- Otherwise set allJournalLinesIntent to an empty string.\n\n## Output schema:\n{\"userQuestion\":\"complete detail question\",\"queryTitle\":\"short title\",\"allJournalLinesIntent\":\"allJournalLines|\",\"sortAction\":\"none\",\"sortBy\":[]}\n\n## Sort intent rules:\n- sortAction must be \"none\", \"replace\", or \"append\".\n- Use \"none\" when the current USER input has no explicit sort/order intent.\n- Use \"append\" only when the current USER asks to add/include/also sort fields.\n- Use \"replace\" when the current USER asks for explicit sort/order without add/include/also wording.\n- sortBy contains only explicit sort fields from the current USER input, in user-mentioned order.\n- Each sortBy item must be {\"field\":\"<user wording>\",\"order\":\"asc|desc\"}; default order is \"asc\", use \"desc\" only for explicit descending/reverse/latest/highest/largest first.\n- Do not populate sortBy for carried-forward sort or implicit breakdown sorting.\n\n## Hard rules:\n- Output exactly one JSON object\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No nulls\n- No trailing text"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Returns invalid Insights query spoof state errors.",
            "name": "Return Reused Query Error"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "FIN_GL_RETURN_REUSED_QUERY_ERROR",
          "id": "linear_1807_return_journal_query_spoof_error",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "linear_1807_returnValue",
              "name": "returnValue",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_BUILD_REUSED_QUERY_ERROR.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "RETURN"
