        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Classifies whether the journal summary analytic-view path needs a new query and whether COA breakdown is requested.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Determine Analytic View Flow Requirements"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1220_construct_journal_breakdown"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYTIC_VIEW_FLOW_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "linear_1017_determine_coa_breakdown_needed",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776970051649_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict flow classifier for a Journals Inquiry Assistant analytic-view path.\n\nYour job is to decide whether the current journal-summary request needs a new analytic-view query, and whether it includes a COA breakdown request.\nReturn exactly one JSON object and nothing else.\n\nInputs:\nUSER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.userInput}}\n\nCHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.chatHistory}}\n\nTURN_CONTEXT:\n{\n  ledgerCategory: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.ledgerCategory}},\n  selectedHierarchies: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.selectedHierarchies}},\n  scopeChange: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.scopeChange}}\n}\n\nACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  analyticViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed}},\n  businessViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}},\n  queryResponse: {{$context.$variables.queryResponse}},\n  dataResponse: {{$context.$variables.dataResponse}},\n  coaBreakdown: {{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}}\n}\n\nOutput shape:\n{\"scopeChanged\":true,\"breakdownRequired\":false,\"sortRequired\":false,\"sortAction\":\"none\",\"sortBy\":[],\"varianceAction\":\"preserve\"}\n\nDefinitions:\n- scopeChanged true means the workflow must generate a fresh journal summary analytic-view query before data retrieval.\n- scopeChanged false means the active journal summary analytic-view query can be reused.\n- breakdownRequired true means the current user message asks for COA segment breakdown, drill, expansion, child rows, leaf output, or detail output over a COA dimension.\n- sortRequired true means the current user message explicitly asks to sort or order the result.\n- sortRequired false means the current user message has no explicit sort/order-by request. Do not set it true for implicit breakdown sorting.\n- sortAction must be \"none\", \"replace\", or \"append\".\n- sortAction \"none\" means the current user message has no explicit sort/order-by request.\n- sortAction \"replace\" means the current user message asks for a new sort/order-by set without add/include/also wording.\n- sortAction \"append\" means the current user message asks to add/include/also sort fields to the existing sort.\n- sortBy contains only explicit sort fields from the current user message. Do not carry forward prior sort fields here.\n- varianceAction must be \"enable\", \"disable\", or \"preserve\".\n- varianceAction \"enable\" means the current user asks for plain journal variance or comparison across fiscal periods.\n- varianceAction \"disable\" means the current user explicitly asks to remove variance, stop comparing, or show without variance.\n- varianceAction \"preserve\" means the current user does not change variance behavior.\n- COA dimensions include company, balancing segment, cost center, cost centre, account, natural account, intercompany, and other chart-of-accounts segments.\n- Journal attributes are not COA dimensions. Journal source, journal category, batch, ledger, period, accounting date, legal entity, business unit, status, and approval status are query-defining journal attributes.\n\nPure COA breakdown rule:\n- A pure COA breakdown request is not a scope change when there is an active journal summary analytic-view query. Return scopeChanged false and breakdownRequired true.\n- Pure COA breakdown requests include break down, split, group, drill, expand, show child rows, show leaf output, show detail output, or show contributors by a COA segment.\n- COA member values inside a breakdown request are breakdown members, not query filters. Examples: expand company 5000, drill into account 11010, break down cost center 300, show leaf company 11.\n- Do not mark scopeChanged true merely because a COA segment value is mentioned as the member of a COA breakdown or drill request.\n\nPure sort rule:\n- If the current message has explicit sort/order intent and no filter/scope change, return scopeChanged false and sortRequired true.\n- If explicit sort/order intent is combined with a filter/scope change, return scopeChanged true and sortRequired true.\n- Breakdown-only is not explicit sort: keep sortRequired false and sortBy empty for implicit breakdown sorting.\n- For explicit sort, set sortAction to \"append\" only for add/include/also wording; otherwise use \"replace\". If no explicit sort, use \"none\".\n- For explicit sort, populate sortBy in user-mentioned field order as {\"field\":\"<user wording>\",\"order\":\"asc|desc\"}; default order is \"asc\", use \"desc\" only for explicit descending/reverse/latest/highest/largest first.\n\nNon-COA breakdown rule:\n- A non-COA breakdown or grouping is query-defining. Return scopeChanged true and breakdownRequired false unless the same request also includes a separate COA breakdown.\n- Non-COA breakdowns include journal source, journal category, batch, ledger, period, accounting date, legal entity, business unit, posting status, approval status, and other non-COA journal attributes.\n\nReturn scopeChanged true if any rule below is satisfied:\n- ACTIVE_STATE is empty, missing, unusable, or has no queryResponse.\n- ACTIVE_STATE has a businessViewNameUsed value.\n- ACTIVE_STATE has no analyticViewNameUsed value.\n- analyticViewNameUsed is not ora_erp_core_accountedTransactions_runtime_x__JournalSummary.\n- TURN_CONTEXT.scopeChange is boolean true or the string \"true\".\n- selectedHierarchies changed relative to the active query or the current turn provides a hierarchy override that is not already reflected in the active query.\n- The request is a balance-to-journal follow-up, such as journals contributing to a balance, transactions behind a balance, journals behind a balance, balance breakdown by journals, or list journals for the above balance context.\n- The request changes data grain, especially switching from summary or aggregate journal output to journal details, journal lines, full journal entries, action logs, or record-level journal inquiry.\n- The request adds, removes, or changes any concrete filter-bearing value that is not merely the member of a pure COA breakdown request. Filter-bearing values include ledger, period, accounting date, date range, currency explicitly mentioned by a USER message, journal source, journal category, batch, journal name, legal entity, business unit, posting status, approval status, action status, line description, account, company, cost center, balancing segment, natural account, intercompany, account combination, or any other COA segment value used as a filter.\n- The request asks for a specific journal or batch identifier, a specific set from prior results, or references such as the above journals, these batches, first journal, this journal, selected journal, or journal 12345.\n- The request asks for breakdown or grouping by a non-COA journal attribute such as journal source, journal category, batch, ledger, period, accounting date, legal entity, or business unit.\n- The request mixes a non-COA journal-attribute breakdown with a COA segment breakdown or filter, such as breakdown by journal source for company 11 or breakdown by category for company 22.\n- The request enables or disables plain journal variance or comparison across fiscal periods.\n\nReturn scopeChanged false only when active filters and selected hierarchies can be reused and the user asks only for COA segment-level breakdown, drill, expand, split, child rows, leaf output, or detail output over a COA dimension, pure sort/order-by behavior, or both, without changing filters and without requesting a specific journal or batch detail.\n\nSet sortRequired true only for explicit sort/order-by intent in the current user message. Set sortRequired false when sorting is only implied by a breakdown request.\n\nSet breakdownRequired true when the current user asks to break down, split, group, drill, expand, show child rows, show leaf output, show detail output, or show contributors by a COA segment. Set it true even when scopeChanged is also true.\n\nSet breakdownRequired false when the request has no COA breakdown request or asks only for non-COA journal-attribute grouping.\n\nSet varianceAction:\n- \"enable\" for plain journal variance or comparison requests using wording such as variance, compare, compared to, comparison, vs, versus, difference between periods, change between periods, period-over-period, MoM, QoQ, or YoY for journal activity or journal amounts.\n- \"disable\" for no variance, without variance, remove variance, stop comparing, or equivalent wording.\n- \"preserve\" otherwise.\n\nDo not extract or encode variance amount or variance percent threshold conditions. Journal variance support is plain variance only.\n\nTie-break rules:\n- Query-defining non-COA changes take precedence over COA breakdown intent.\n- Pure COA breakdown-only follow-ups reuse the active query and only change coaBreakdown during data retrieval.\n- Never reuse a prior query when returning scopeChanged true.\n\nHard rules:\n- Output exactly one JSON object.\n- No markdown.\n- No explanation.\n- No trailing text.\n- No nulls.\n- scopeChanged, breakdownRequired, and sortRequired are required booleans.\n- sortAction is required and must be \"none\", \"replace\", or \"append\".\n- sortBy is required and must be an array.\n- varianceAction is required and must be \"enable\", \"disable\", or \"preserve\"."
            },
            {
              "id": "1776970051649_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Decides whether to rebuild detail filters.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Classify Detail Scope Change"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1020_determine_bv"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_DETAIL_SCOPE_CHANGE_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "linear_1203_determine_journal_detail_scope_change",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "linear_1203_determine_journal_detail_scope_change_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict scope-change detector for a Journals Inquiry Assistant detail flow.\n\nYour job is to determine whether the current detail request must rebuild business-view filters or can reuse the active query.\nReturn exactly one boolean and nothing else.\n\nInputs:\nCHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.chatHistory}}\n\nUSER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.userInput}}\n\n\n\n\nTURN_CONTEXT:\n{\n  selectedHierarchies: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.selectedHierarchies}},\n  scopeChange: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.scopeChange}}\n}\n\nDETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYZE_DETAIL_AND_LINES_INTENT.$output}}\n\nACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  analyticViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed}},\n  businessViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}},\n  queryResponse: {{$context.$variables.queryResponse}},\n  dataResponse: {{$context.$variables.dataResponse}},\n  coaBreakdown: {{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}}\n}\n\nReturn true when:\n- ACTIVE_STATE is empty, missing, unusable, or has no queryResponse.\n- TURN_CONTEXT.scopeChange is string \"true\" or boolean true.\n- selectedHierarchies changed relative to the active query.\n- USER_INPUT changes the requested journal detail grain or view intent, such as switching between journal header detail, line detail, full journal entries, or action-log/history detail.\n- USER_INPUT adds, removes, or changes any concrete filter value, journal/batch identifier, period, ledger, date, currency explicitly mentioned by a USER message, source, category, status, approval status, action status, COA segment value, account combination, line description, or line-level amount condition.\n- USER_INPUT has explicit sort/order-by intent together with any filter, identifier, grain, selected hierarchy, or detail-intent change.\n- USER_INPUT asks for a specific journal/batch identifier or references a specific set from prior results such as the above journals, these batches, first journal, this journal, selected journal, or journal 12345.\n- USER_INPUT asks for journal details, journal lines, journal entries, full journal entry, full journal details, all journal lines, full journal lines, or line-level data for a specific journal/batch or set of journals/batches.\n- USER_INPUT is a balance-to-journal follow-up. Always rebuild.\n\nReturn false only when the existing detail query can be reused without changing filters, grain, selected hierarchies, identifiers, or requested detail intent. Pure sort/order-by requests are presentation-only and must return false.\n\nTreat direct sorting/ordering intent, sort direction, ranking direction, and add/include/also sort wording as explicit sort/order-by intent.\n\nHard rules:\n- Output exactly true or false\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No trailing text\n- No nulls"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"boolean\"}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Normalizes journal summary analytic-view flow requirements before routing.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Parse Analytic View Flow Requirements",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const parseObject = (value) => {\n  if (value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return value;\n  }\n  if (typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() !== \"\") {\n    try {\n      const parsedValue = JSON.parse(value);\n      if (parsedValue !== null && typeof parsedValue === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(parsedValue)) {\n        return parsedValue;\n      }\n    } catch (error) {}\n  }\n  const empty = {};\n  return empty;\n};\n\nconst asBoolean = (value) => value === true || String(value || \"\").trim().toLowerCase() === \"true\";\nconst normalizeSortAction = (value, sortRequired) => {\n  if (!sortRequired) {\n    return \"none\";\n  }\n\n  const action = String(value || \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n  return action === \"append\" ? \"append\" : \"replace\";\n};\nconst normalizeSortBy = (value) => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  const result = [];\n  const seen = new Set();\n\n  for (const item of value) {\n    if (!item || typeof item !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(item)) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    const field = String(item.field || \"\").trim();\n    if (!field) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    const orderText = String(item.order || \"asc\").trim().toLowerCase();\n    const order = orderText === \"desc\" || orderText === \"descending\" ? \"desc\" : \"asc\";\n    const key = field.toLowerCase();\n\n    if (!seen.has(key)) {\n      seen.add(key);\n      result.push({ field, order });\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n};\nconst summaryAnalyticView = \"ora_erp_core_accountedTransactions_runtime_x__JournalSummary\";\nconst parserResult = $context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT?.$output?.result ?? {};\nconst classifierOutput = parseObject($context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYTIC_VIEW_FLOW_CLASSIFIER?.$output);\nconst activeAnalyticViewName = String($context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed || parserResult.analyticViewNameUsed || \"\");\nconst activeBusinessViewName = String($context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed || parserResult.businessViewNameUsed || \"\");\nconst priorRequestType = activeAnalyticViewName ? \"SUMMARY\" : activeBusinessViewName ? \"DETAIL\" : \"\";\nconst priorIsJournalsSummary = activeAnalyticViewName === summaryAnalyticView;\nconst metadataSegments = $context.$variables.queryResponse?.metadata?.chartOfAccounts?.segments;\nconst coaMetadataAvailable =\n  metadataSegments !== null &&\n  typeof metadataSegments === \"object\" &&\n  !Array.isArray(metadataSegments) &&\n  Object.keys(metadataSegments).length > 0;\n\nlet scopeChanged = asBoolean(classifierOutput.scopeChanged);\nif (!priorIsJournalsSummary) {\n  scopeChanged = true;\n}\n\nconst sortRequired = asBoolean(classifierOutput.sortRequired);\nconst sortAction = normalizeSortAction(classifierOutput.sortAction, sortRequired);\n\nconst res = {\n  scopeChanged,\n  breakdownRequired: asBoolean(classifierOutput.breakdownRequired),\n  sortRequired,\n  sortAction,\n  sortBy: sortRequired ? normalizeSortBy(classifierOutput.sortBy) : [],\n  varianceAction: classifierOutput.varianceAction,\n  priorRequestType,\n  coaMetadataAvailable\n};\n\nreturn res;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1019_if_scope_change"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_ANALYTIC_VIEW_FLOW_REQUIREMENTS",
          "id": "linear_1220_construct_journal_breakdown",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Chooses the journal detail business view.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Choose Detail View"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1204_resolve_journal_detail_analysis"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_CHOOSE_DETAIL_VIEW",
          "id": "linear_1020_determine_bv",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776125399576_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict journal business-view selector.\n\nYour job is to select exactly one journal business view for a Journals Inquiry Assistant detail request.\n\nReturn exactly one minified JSON object and nothing else.\n\nSet the businessView based on DETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS.userQuestion, using the purpose, coverage, precedence, and exclusions defined in the Business view selection section below. Do not use raw user input (USER_INPUT) for business-view selection.\n\n## Inputs:\nCHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.chatHistory}}\n\nUSER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.userInput}}\n\nDETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYZE_DETAIL_AND_LINES_INTENT.$output}}\n\nREPHRASED_QUESTION:\nDETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS.userQuestion\n\nDETAIL_SCOPE_CHANGE:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_DETAIL_SCOPE_CHANGE_CLASSIFIER.$output}}\n\nACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  analyticViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed}},\n  businessViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}},\n  queryResponse: {{$context.$variables.queryResponse}},\n  dataResponse: {{$context.$variables.dataResponse}},\n  coaBreakdown: {{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}}\n}\n\n## Business view precedence:\n- Before applying the numbered precedence order, if DETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS.userQuestion asks for who performed, who needs to perform, or when a journal/batch action happened, choose journalActionLogDetails unless the same question explicitly asks for journal line-level or COA-level data.\n\nEvaluate in this exact order and stop at the first match:\n1. generalLedgerJournalDetail\n2. journalActionLogDetails\n3. journalHeaderDetail\n\n## Business view selection:\n1. generalLedgerJournalDetail\n   - businessObject = JournalLine\n   - module = oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\n   - Purpose: Provides journal information at journal-line granularity.\n   - Select only when DETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS.userQuestion has any line-level or Chart of Accounts (COA) intent.\n   - Line-level or COA intent includes:\n        - COA segment names/values (e.g., `company 3000` or `marketing division` or `account 1234`).\n        - Account combinations (e.g., `01-110-1110-1111`, `3111.01.112233.0000`).\n        - Line description, line-level debit or credit amounts, currency conversion type or rate, journal lines, journals contributing to balance, line details, or similar line-level intent.\n   - Also select when DETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS.allJournalLinesIntent is \"allJournalLines\".\n   - Precedence: if any COA or line-level cue exists, choose generalLedgerJournalDetail even if header, action log, who, or when attributes are also mentioned.\n   - Who/when attribute routing:\n        - Created by, updated by, creation date, update date, and posted date may exist in both header and line business views.\n        - Select generalLedgerJournalDetail for these who/when attributes when line-level or COA intent is present.\n        - Posted by belongs to journalActionLogDetails when line-level or COA intent is absent.\n        - If posted-by intent appears with line-level or COA intent, generalLedgerJournalDetail takes precedence.\n   - Do not select this business view if:\n        - the rephrased question is only about action/history/workflow and has no line-level or COA intent.\n        - the rephrased question is only about journal header or batch attributes without line-level or COA intent.\n\n2. journalActionLogDetails\n   - businessObject = JournalActionLog\n   - module = oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\n   - Purpose: Provides information about workflow, action events, approval, rejection, withdrawal, posted-by, and action history.\n   - Select only when generalLedgerJournalDetail does not match and DETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS.userQuestion requires journal workflow/action history or posted-by information.\n   - Workflow/action history includes:\n        - `who` performed an action, for example `approved by X`, `With whom is it pending approval?`, `who are the approvers`, `who approved`, or `posted by`.\n        - `when` a workflow action happened, for example `withdrawn yesterday`, `rejected 2 weeks ago`, or `approved in last 7 days`.\n        - history, audit, lifecycle, or workflow-trace intent.\n   - Exceptions:\n        - `created` or `updated` with `who` -> journalHeaderDetail when line-level or COA intent is absent.\n        - `created`, `updated`, or `posted` with `when` -> journalHeaderDetail when line-level or COA intent is absent.\n        - Status-only requests without line-level or COA intent like `show approved journals`, `show journals pending approval`, `show posted/unposted journals` -> journalHeaderDetail.\n\n3. journalHeaderDetail\n   - businessObject = JournalHeader\n   - module = oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\n   - Purpose: Provides information at the journal header / batch granularity (NO COA or Line-level intent).\n   - Default selection when generalLedgerJournalDetail and journalActionLogDetails do not match.\n   - Select when DETAIL_QUESTION_AND_LINES_ANALYSIS.userQuestion requires journal header or batch information without journal-line, accounting-distribution, account-combination, COA-segment, or balance-drilldown context.\n   - Header or batch information includes journal name, batch name, source, category, ledger, ledger set, legal entity, period, accounting date, posted date, creation date/created by, update date/updated by, posting status, approval status, header-level totals, or batch-level totals.\n   - Who/when attribute routing:\n        - Select journalHeaderDetail for created by, updated by, creation date, update date, or posted date when line-level or COA intent is absent.\n        - Do not select journalHeaderDetail for posted by when line-level or COA intent is absent; posted by belongs to journalActionLogDetails.\n   - Exceptions:\n        - Do not select when journal-line, journal-detail, account-combination, COA-segment, or balance-drilldown context is present.\n        - Do not select when explicit workflow/action-history intent or posted-by intent is present and generalLedgerJournalDetail does not match.\n\n## Output schema:\n{\"businessView\":\"generalLedgerJournalDetail|journalActionLogDetails|journalHeaderDetail\",\"businessObject\":\"JournalLine|JournalActionLog|JournalHeader\",\"module\":\"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\"}\n\n## Hard rules:\n- Output exactly one JSON object\n- No markdown\n- No explanation\n- No extra keys\n- No nulls\n- No trailing text"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"oneOf\":[{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"businessView\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"generalLedgerJournalDetail\"]},\"businessObject\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"JournalLine\"]},\"module\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\"]}},\"required\":[\"businessView\",\"businessObject\",\"module\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"businessView\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"journalActionLogDetails\"]},\"businessObject\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"JournalActionLog\"]},\"module\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\"]}},\"required\":[\"businessView\",\"businessObject\",\"module\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"businessView\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"journalHeaderDetail\"]},\"businessObject\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"JournalHeader\"]},\"module\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\"]}},\"required\":[\"businessView\",\"businessObject\",\"module\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}]}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Routes summary requests by filter reuse decision.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Route Summary Scope Change"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "linear_1016_rephrase_user_question",
            "false": "add_false_linear_1019_if_scope_change"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_CONDITION_IF_SCOPE_CHANGE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "linear_1901_breakdown_request_check",
          "id": "linear_1019_if_scope_change",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776198413013_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_ANALYTIC_VIEW_FLOW_REQUIREMENTS.$output.result.scopeChanged}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Normalizes detail view, question, line intent, and scope.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Resolve Detail Analysis",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const asString = (value) => (typeof value === \"string\" ? value.trim() : \"\");\nconst emptyObject = () => JSON.parse(\"{}\");\nconst parseJsonObject = (value) => {\n  if (value !== null && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value)) return value;\n  if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n    try {\n      const parsed = JSON.parse(value);\n      return parsed !== null && typeof parsed === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : {};\n    } catch (error) {\n      return emptyObject();\n    }\n  }\n  return emptyObject();\n};\nconst parseBoolean = (value) => {\n  if (value === true || value === false) return value;\n  if (value && typeof value === \"object\" && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(value, \"result\")) {\n    return parseBoolean(value.result);\n  }\n  const text = asString(value).toLowerCase();\n  return text === \"true\" || text === \"yes\" || text === \"y\";\n};\nconst normalizeSortAction = (value, sortBy) => {\n  const action = asString(value).toLowerCase();\n  if (!Array.isArray(sortBy) || sortBy.length === 0 || action === \"none\") {\n    return \"none\";\n  }\n  return action === \"append\" ? \"append\" : \"replace\";\n};\nconst normalizeSortBy = (value) => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  const result = [];\n  const seen = new Set();\n\n  for (const item of value) {\n    if (!item || typeof item !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(item)) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    const field = asString(item.field);\n    if (!field) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    const orderText = asString(item.order).toLowerCase();\n    const order = orderText === \"desc\" || orderText === \"descending\" ? \"desc\" : \"asc\";\n    const key = field.toLowerCase();\n\n    if (!seen.has(key)) {\n      seen.add(key);\n      result.push({ field, order });\n    }\n  }\n\n  return result;\n};\n\nconst selected = parseJsonObject($context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_CHOOSE_DETAIL_VIEW?.$output);\nconst viewMap = {\n  generalLedgerJournalDetail: {\n    businessView: \"generalLedgerJournalDetail\",\n    businessObject: \"JournalLine\",\n    module: \"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\"\n  },\n  journalActionLogDetails: {\n    businessView: \"journalActionLogDetails\",\n    businessObject: \"JournalActionLog\",\n    module: \"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\"\n  },\n  journalHeaderDetail: {\n    businessView: \"journalHeaderDetail\",\n    businessObject: \"JournalHeader\",\n    module: \"oraErpCoreAccountingEntries\"\n  }\n};\nconst mapped = viewMap[asString(selected.businessView)] ?? viewMap.journalHeaderDetail;\nconst detailAnalysis = parseJsonObject($context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_ANALYZE_DETAIL_AND_LINES_INTENT?.$output);\nconst userQuestion = asString(detailAnalysis.userQuestion) || asString($context.$system.$inputMessage);\nconst queryTitle = asString(detailAnalysis.queryTitle) || userQuestion;\nconst allJournalLinesIntent = asString(detailAnalysis.allJournalLinesIntent) === \"allJournalLines\" ? \"allJournalLines\" : \"\";\nconst sortBy = normalizeSortBy(detailAnalysis.sortBy);\nconst sortAction = normalizeSortAction(detailAnalysis.sortAction, sortBy);\n\nconst returnObj = {\n  ...mapped,\n  userQuestion,\n  queryTitle,\n  allJournalLinesIntent,\n  sortAction,\n  sortBy,\n  scopeChange: parseBoolean($context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_DETAIL_SCOPE_CHANGE_CLASSIFIER?.$output)\n};\n\nreturn returnObj;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1021_set_bv_object"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_CODE_RESOLVE_DETAIL_ANALYSIS",
          "id": "linear_1204_resolve_journal_detail_analysis",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Creates the summary question for filter generation.",
            "errorNodeId": "linear_1305_route_runtime_error_response",
            "name": "Rephrase Summary Question"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "linear_1221_resolve_journal_summary_analysis"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_REPHRASE_SUMMARY_QUESTION",
          "id": "linear_1016_rephrase_user_question",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776969882238_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Role & Objective\nYou are a strict question rephraser for a Journals Inquiry Assistant summary flow.\n\nYour job is to build one complete, self-contained natural-language journal question from the current USER input and prior USER inputs.\nReturn exactly one question string and nothing else.\n\n## Inputs:\nCHAT_HISTORY:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.chatHistory}}\n\nUSER_INPUT:\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.userInput}}\n\nTURN_CONTEXT:\n{\n  ledgerContext: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.ledgerContext}},\n  ledgerCategory: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.ledgerCategory}},\n  selectedHierarchies: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_GL_CODE_PARSE_INPUT.$output.result.turnContext.selectedHierarchies}}\n}\n\nACTIVE_STATE:\n{\n  analyticViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.analyticViewNameUsed}},\n  businessViewNameUsed: {{$context.$variables.businessViewNameUsed}},\n  queryResponse: {{$context.$variables.queryResponse}},\n  dataResponse: {{$context.$variables.dataResponse}},\n  coaBreakdown: {{$context.$variables.coaBreakdown}}\n}\n\n## Core behavior:\n- Rephrase, do not interpret.\n- Frame one meaningful, complete journal question based on the current USER intent, preserving the current USER entities, filters, conditions, and intent as-is. For short follow-ups, preserve the meaning but do not preserve fragment wording.\n- Add only missing context from prior USER inputs when still applicable and not replaced, contradicted, or made irrelevant by the current USER input.\n- Do not paraphrase, normalize, infer, map, summarize, group, resolve, or transform USER terms.\n- Do not include technical/context JSON.\n\n## First question behavior:\n- If this is the first USER question in the conversation, return the USER_INPUT as-is as the final question, except replace double quotes with single quotes.\n- Do not add context from prior messages, TURN_CONTEXT, ACTIVE_STATE, assistant messages, tool outputs, or result data for the first question.\n\n## Source of truth:\n- Use ONLY values explicitly mentioned in current or prior USER inputs.\n- TURN_CONTEXT and ACTIVE_STATE may be used only to detect flow state when needed; they must not be used as sources for filters, values, rows, currencies, ledgers, periods, amounts, identifiers, or wording in the final question.\n- DO NOT pick values from AI-generated titles, headlines, displayed rows, result rows, row headers, child/detail rows, parent rows, intent-confirmation blocks, tool outputs, currentLevelAvData, childLevelAvData, measure result values, prior returned table cells, or assistant text.\n- Current USER input has highest precedence for fields/entities/anchors it mentions. Add new current fields, replace prior values only for the same field, and keep unrelated prior USER-mentioned filters unless the current USER explicitly removes or changes them.\n- The latest USER-mentioned value for the same field/entity replaces earlier values unless the user asks to include multiple values.\n- Never invent missing filters, anchors, dates, ledgers, currencies, statuses, COA values, or identifiers.\n\n## Carry-forward rules:\n- For follow-ups, carry forward only applicable scope anchors explicitly mentioned in prior USER inputs when the current USER input is silent about that same field/anchor. A current USER value for one field/anchor replaces only that same field/anchor and does not remove unrelated prior USER-mentioned filters.\n- Scope anchors include but not limited to: accounting period/date/date ranges, ledger, journal/approval status, source, category, legal entity, currency if user-mentioned, COA filters, journal/batch identifiers, amount filters, breakdown dimensions, and explicit sort/order-by fields and order.\n- Carry forward the prior USER-mentioned base journal intent when needed, such as journal activity, summary, journals, details, lines, or entries.\n- If the current USER input corrects prior USER wording, such as \"I meant X not Y\", reframe the still-applicable prior USER question with the correction applied and do not include the correction phrase itself in the final question.\n- Preserve existing journal-attribute filters and breakdowns unless the current USER replaces, removes, contradicts, or changes them.\n- Preserve explicit user-mentioned sort/order-by fields and order unless the current USER replaces, removes, contradicts, or changes them. Do not add implicit sort wording for breakdown requests.\n- If the current USER adds values using wording such as also/include/both, accumulate those values.\n- If values conflict, use the current USER input value.\n- Ledger and accounting period/date filters must be carried forward only when explicitly mentioned in prior USER inputs and the current USER input is silent about them, unless the current USER explicitly changes or drops them.\n- Do not carry forward ledger or accounting period/date values merely because they appear in TURN_CONTEXT, ACTIVE_STATE, assistant text, tool output, or result data.\n\n## Rephrasing guardrails:\nWhen framing or rephrasing the current user question:\n\nDO NOT:\n- Add clarifications, explanations, parenthetical expansions, synonyms, semantic equivalents, qualifiers, business terms, or inferred filters.\n- Generalize or specialize any term.\n- Convert detail/list requests into summary/aggregate/breakdown requests, or summary/aggregate/breakdown requests into detail/list requests unless the user explicitly asks for it.\n- Convert a currency descriptor into a currency breakdown unless the user explicitly asks to break down, group, summarize, or show by currency.\n- Derive or carry forward filters from prior headlines, displayed table rows, row headers, child/detail rows, parent rows, tool result rows, `childLevelAvData`, `currentLevelAvData`, or measure result values.\n- Alter, split, tokenize, or reinterpret text enclosed in single ('...') or double (\"...\") quotes (treat the full quoted string as an atomic identifier and preserve it exactly in the rephrased question, except that double quote characters must be replaced with single quote characters in the final output).\n- Leave out user-specified values, including COA segment values, batch names, journal names, transaction numbers, journal source, journal category, account combinations, currency terms, or line descriptions, unless explicitly requested to be dropped.\n- Drop or replace existing journal-attribute breakdown/grouping dimensions unless the user explicitly says to replace/remove them.\n- Rewrite, normalize, or substitute status/control phrases. Preserve these phrases EXACTLY as stated in the user input or valid carried context, such as \"without approvals\", \"not approved\", \"unapproved\", \"not posted\", \"pending\", \"posted\", etc.\n- Add posting status unless it was explicitly mentioned in current or still-applicable prior USER input, except when the balance-to-journal follow-up rule explicitly allows adding \"posted journals\" or \"posted journal lines\".\n- Append filters or statuses as detached trailing fragments. The final output must be one natural, grammatically complete question.\n- Include entered currency, ledger currency, currency code, currency symbols, or any currency-related wording while rephrasing UNLESS that exact currency wording was explicitly mentioned in the current or prior USER input. Do not infer it from balance responses, intent-confirmation text, tool filters, result rows, monetary templates, ledger currency, or examples.\n- Carry forward terms like aggregate/summary/total from prior user inputs unless explicitly mentioned by the user in the current input or required by an active prior USER-requested breakdown/summary context.\n- Carry forward prior COA segment filters, account combination filters, or COA segment breakdowns for journal details/lines/entries for a specific journal/batch unless the current user explicitly repeats them.\n\nONLY:\n- Fix only minimal grammar or word-order issues required to make the final output a valid question, without changing USER wording, business terms, filters, values, conditions, or intent.\n- Carry forward filters, entities, conditions, and breakdowns exactly as stated, subject to these guardrails.\n- Apply entity replacement across USER messages first: the most recent USER-mentioned value for the same field/entity replaces any earlier value unless the user explicitly asks to include multiple values.\n- Preserve quoted text as one atomic identifier, except that double quote characters must be replaced with single quote characters in the final output.\n- ALWAYS replace any double quotes (\"..\") in the final userQuestion with single quotes ('..') and NEVER introduce double quotes in the final userQuestion.\n\n## Calendar and date handling:\n- Preserve temporal expressions exactly as stated.\n- Do not resolve relative dates or periods into absolute dates, calendar ranges, accounting periods, or labels.\n- Do not convert fiscal-period-shaped values such as Feb-26, Mar-26, or May-26 into calendar dates or date ranges during rephrasing.\n- If the USER names a date field, preserve that date-field wording.\n- If the current USER input is silent about period/date range or ledger, carry forward prior applicable USER-mentioned period/date range or ledger.\n- Do not default period/date range from current date, system date, context JSON, or tool output.\n\n## Balance-to-journal follow-up rules:\n- Apply this section only when the current request is a balance-to-journal follow-up and a prior successful balance response exists in chat history.\n- A prior successful balance response may be used only to detect that the current request is a balance-to-journal follow-up. It must not be used as a source for filters, values, rows, currencies, ledgers, periods, amounts, or identifiers.\n- Remove any numeric comparison, threshold, or range conditions on balance/amount measures that originated in prior turns unless the current USER input specifies a new journal amount condition.\n- Remove inherited amount expressions using comparators such as greater than, more than, over, at least, less than, under, at most, between, equals, not equals, and operators like >, <, >=, <=, =, !=.\n- Remove inherited amount expressions with currency symbols/codes before or after the number, optional spaces, and number formatting such as commas, periods, or thin spaces. Examples: greater than 5000, lesser than 3,000 USD, > $3,000, between EUR 2,000 and 5,000, at most GBP 4,500.50.\n- If the current USER specifies a new journal amount condition, KEEP it.\n- For balance-to-journal follow-ups, carry forward prior USER-mentioned non-amount balance scope filters, including account/COA, company, period/date, ledger, legal entity, and currency wording when explicitly user-mentioned, unless the current USER replaces that same field. Do not carry forward amount filters unless the current USER specifies a new journal amount condition.\n- Carry forward currency wording only when explicitly mentioned in a USER input.\n- Do not reinterpret balance amount conditions as journal amount conditions.\n- Do not carry currency from balance context unless currency was explicitly mentioned in current or prior USER inputs/messages.\n- Do not use balance result rows, headlines, tool outputs, intent-confirmation text, context JSON, or measure values as journal filters.\n- The rephrased question must preserve the user’s current input and intent, plus only valid carried-forward context.\n\n## Journal status for balance-to-journal follow-ups ONLY\n- Apply this section ONLY when the current input is a journal-related follow-up from a prior successful BALANCE response.\n- Do NOT apply this section when the prior successful response was already journal-related, including journal amounts, activity, net activity, summaries, batches, lines, details, or entries.\n- Status handling:\n\t- Every valid balance-to-journal follow-up must include a posting status.\n\t- If the current USER input mentions a posting status, preserve it exactly.\n\t- Otherwise, add the default status \"posted\".\n- Object handling for valid balance-to-journal follow-ups:\n\t- Preserve the journal object requested by the current USER input.\n\t- For example:\n\t\t- If the USER asks for Journal Batches, use \"posted Journal Batches\".\n\t\t- If the USER asks for Journals or contributing journals, use \"posted journals\".\n\t\t- If the USER asks for Journal Lines, Journal Details, Journal Entries, line details, or line descriptions, use \"posted journal lines\".\n\t\t- If the USER does not specify a journal object and asks usage/detail questions such as \"where was this used\", \"show usage\", \"show details\", or \"show/list contributing details\" and if the current or prior user question has COA or line level intent then also use \"posted journal lines\".\n- Hard boundary:\n\t- Never infer or add \"posted\" outside valid balance-to-journal follow-ups.\n\t- Never replace, normalize, or override a USER-mentioned posting status.\n\t- Never use assistant messages, result rows, table headers, tool outputs, ACTIVE_STATE, or TURN_CONTEXT as a source for posting status.\n\n## Output requirements:\n- Output only the final question text.\n- Replace any double quotes with single quotes.\n- Do not include labels, JSON, markdown, comments, or trailing text.\n- Do not include chartOfAccountsId, processExecutionId, conversationId, selectedHierarchies JSON, raw Context JSON, toolTimeStamp, or internal field names unless explicitly requested by the user."
            },
